# Git attributes — line-ending enforcement
# Created: 2026-04-22 (Phase B continuity bridge implementation)
#
# Context: Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true will reintroduce CRLF line
# endings into shell scripts on every checkout. WSL bash fails hard on CRLF
# ("$'\r': command not found"). Phase B scan-secrets.sh --stdin is invoked from
# continuity-append.mjs running under WSL (Hermes-Telegram surface), so durable
# LF on scripts/*.sh is required.

scripts/*.sh text eol=lf

# Git hooks are bash and are executed from the WORKING COPY, under WSL/Linux as
# well as Git Bash. Blobs are already stored LF; the exposure is the checkout —
# on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, an uncovered path is written to disk with
# CRLF and then fails under WSL with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M".
# That is the same reasoning as the scripts/*.sh rule above, and .githooks/ was
# simply never covered. Added 2026-08-21 with the Rule 42 pre-push gate.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
